From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:48:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_smbx: don't set the float voltage above
 the maximum

The float voltage register counts 7.5 mV steps from 3.4875 V. The driver
adds one step after dividing, so a battery whose maximum design voltage
is a whole number of steps, such as 4.35 V, is charged 7.5 mV above it:
0x74 instead of 0x73. When it isn't a whole number of steps the result
rounds up instead of down. Either way the float voltage ends up above
the battery's maximum.

Drop the extra step. The downstream driver computes the register the
same way, and 4.35 V now gives the 0x73 it programs.

Fixes: 8648aeb5d7b7 ("power: supply: add Qualcomm PMI8998 SMB2 Charger driver")
Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
index 67fdb43353..f5ebf07886 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -999,7 +999,8 @@ static int smb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return dev_err_probe(chip->dev, rc,
 				     "Failed to init status change work\n");
 
-	rc = (chip->batt_info->voltage_max_design_uv - 3487500) / 7500 + 1;
+	/* 3.4875 V plus 7.5 mV steps, rounded down to stay within the maximum */
+	rc = (chip->batt_info->voltage_max_design_uv - 3487500) / 7500;
 	rc = regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap, chip->base + FLOAT_VOLTAGE_CFG,
 				FLOAT_VOLTAGE_SETTING_MASK, rc);
 	if (rc < 0)
